CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2 - Permissive

Preamble

CERN has developed this licence to promote collaboration among hardware
designers and to provide a legal tool which supports the freedom to use,
study, modify, share and distribute hardware designs and products based on
those designs. Version 2 of the CERN Open Hardware Licence comes in three
variants: this licence, CERN-OHL-P (permissive); and two reciprocal
licences: CERN-OHL-W (weakly reciprocal) and CERN-OHL-S (strongly
reciprocal).

The CERN-OHL-P is copyright CERN 2020. Anyone is welcome to use it, in
unmodified form only.

Use of this Licence does not imply any endorsement by CERN of any Licensor
or their designs nor does it imply any involvement by CERN in their
development.

1 Definitions

  1.1 'Licence' means this CERN-OHL-P.

  1.2 'Compatible Licence' means

       a) any earlier version of the CERN Open Hardware licence, or

       b) any version of the CERN-OHL-S or the CERN-OHL-W, or

       c) any licence which permits You to treat the Source to which it
          applies as licensed under CERN-OHL-S or CERN-OHL-W provided
          that on combination with Source licensed under CERN-OHL-S or
          CERN-OHL-W all licence conditions are met,

  1.3 'Source' means information such as design materials or digital code
      which can be applied to Make or test a Product or to prepare a
      Product for use, Conveyance or sale, regardless of its medium or
      how it is expressed. It may include Notices.

  1.4 'Covered Source' means Source that is explicitly made available
      under this Licence.

  1.5 'Product' means any device, component, work or physical object,
      whether in finished or intermediate form, arising from the use,
      application or processing of Covered Source.

  1.6 'Make' means to create or configure something, whether by
      manufacture, assembly, compiling, loading or applying Covered
      Source or another Product or otherwise.

  1.7 'Available Component' means any part, sub-assembly, library or
      code that:

       a) is licensed to You as Complete Source under a Compatible
          Licence; or

       b) is available, at the time a Product or the Covered Source is
          first Conveyed, to You and any other prospective licensees

            i) as a physical part with sufficient rights and information
               (including any configuration and programming files and
               information about its characteristics and interfaces)
               to enable it either to be Made itself, or to be sourced
               and used to Make the Product; or
           ii) as part of the normal distribution of a tool used to
               design or Make the Product.

  1.8 'Complete Source' means the set of all Source necessary to Make a
      Product, in the preferred form for making modifications, including
      necessary installation and interfacing information both for the
      Product, and for any included Available Components. If the format
      is proprietary, it must also be made available in a format (if the
      proprietary tool can create it) which is viewable with a tool
      available to potential licensees and licensed under a licence
      approved by the Free Software Foundation or the Open Source
      Initiative. Complete Source need not include the Source of any
      Available Component, provided that You include in the Complete
      Source sufficient information to enable a recipient to Make or
      source and use any Available Components to Make the Product.

  1.9 'Source Location' means a location where a Licensor has placed
      Covered Source, and which that Licensor reasonably believes will
      remain easily accessible for at least three years for anyone to
      obtain a digital copy.

 1.10 'Notice' means copyright, acknowledgement and trademark notices,
      Source Location references, modification notices (subsection 3.3(b))
      and all notices that refer to this Licence and to the disclaimer of
      warranties that are included in the Covered Source.

 1.11 'Licensor' means any person who creates or modifies Covered Source.
      A person may be a Licensor and a Licensee at the same time.

 1.12 'Licensee' or 'You' means any person exercising rights under this
      Licence.

 1.13 'Convey' means to communicate to the public or distribute.

2 Applicability

  2.1 This Licence governs the use, copying, modification, Conveying of
      Covered Source and Products, and the Making of Products. By
      exercising any right granted under this Licence, You irrevocably
      accept these terms and conditions.

  2.2 This Licence is granted by the Licensor directly to You, and shall
      apply worldwide and without limitation in time.

  2.3 You shall not attempt to restrict by contract or otherwise the
      rights granted under this Licence to other Licensees.

  2.4 This Licence is not intended to restrict fair use, fair dealing,
      or any other similar right.

3 Copying, Modifying and Conveying Covered Source

  3.1 You may copy and Convey verbatim copies of Covered Source, in any
      medium, provided You retain all Notices.

  3.2 You may modify Covered Source, other than Notices, provided that
      You irrevocably undertake to make that modified Source available
      from a Source Location should You Convey a Product in circumstances
      where the recipient does not otherwise receive a copy of the
      modified Covered Source. In each case subsection 3.3 shall apply.

      You may only delete Notices if they are no longer applicable to the
      corresponding portion of the Covered Source (for example, a Notice
      that is no longer applicable to the modified version).

  3.3 You may Convey modified Covered Source (with the effect that You
      shall also become a Licensor) provided that You:

       a) retain Notices as required in subsection 3.2;

       b) add a Notice to the modified Covered Source stating that You
          have modified it, with the date and brief description of how
          You have modified it;

       c) add a Source Location Notice for the modified Covered Source
          if You Convey in circumstances where the recipient does not
          otherwise receive a copy of the modified Covered Source; and

       d) not attempt to restrict access to (other than to the extent
          permitted by section 3.5) the Source Location of the modified
          Covered Source.

  3.4 You may Convey Covered Source or modified Covered Source without
      restriction provided that You do not Convey a Product.

  3.5 The right to Convey under subsections 3.1, 3.2 and 3.3 does not
      include the right to sublicence. Each time You communicate Covered
      Source or modified Covered Source to a recipient, that recipient
      automatically receives a licence under this Licence. You may not
      impose any further restrictions on the exercise of the licence
      granted to the recipient. You are not responsible for enforcing
      compliance by third parties with this Licence.

  3.6 If You Convey a copy of modified Covered Source with a Compilation,
      You may, to the extent permitted by the licence of the Compilation,
      replace the applicable portions of the licence notice above with
      a different notice so that the Covered Source and the Compilation
      can be exercised under different licences, provided that You do
      not attempt to limit or restrict the right of the recipient to
      obtain, modify and exercise the Covered Source.

4 Making and Conveying Products

You may Make Products, and/or Convey them, provided that You ensure that
the recipient of the Product receives a copy of the Notices. You may make
Products available for others to Make.

